# URME — Cursor Rules

You are working on URME, a Vite 8 + React 18 SPA CRM backed by Supabase
(project ref `rebjykbpmhhaxgpclzsg`) and deployed on Vercel.

## Conventions
- Data access goes through `src/api/base44Client.js` (the `base44.*` adapter shim over
  PostgREST). Do NOT call the Supabase client directly from pages/components; use the adapter.
- Before calling an adapter method, check it exists in `src/api/base44Client.js`. Auth exposes
  `me`, `login`, `register`, `logout(redirectTo?)`, `forgotPassword(email)`,
  `resetPassword(newPassword)`, `onAuthStateChange` — nothing else.
- AI calls use `base44.integrations.Core.InvokeLLM({prompt, response_json_schema, model, temperature})`
  or `src/utils/ai.js` `invokeLLM(...)`. Keep that contract stable; `response_json_schema`,
  `model` and `temperature` are optional and are forwarded to the Edge Function.
- UI uses shadcn/ui + Tailwind. Match existing component patterns.
- Prefer TanStack Query for data fetching/mutations (queryKey per entity).
- Effects that seed default rows must be idempotent (guard on existence, not on an empty cache).

## Guardrails
- NEVER commit `.env.local` or print secret values (API keys, JWTs, service_role key).
- NEVER put secrets in `VITE_*` variables — those ship in the browser bundle. Server-side
  keys (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `XAI_API_KEY`) belong only in Supabase Edge Function env.
- NEVER deploy Edge Functions or run `supabase db push` automatically. Deploys are human-run.
- NEVER run destructive DB or git-history commands against the live project.
- Open PRs for review; do not commit to `main` or merge.

## invoke-llm routing (important)
Multi-provider by caller identity: Michael's user ID → Grok (`XAI_API_KEY`),
all others → Anthropic Claude (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`). The function reads the
Authorization header to resolve the caller and logs `user_id` with token usage.
Keep repo and deployed versions in sync — the repo copy has drifted before.

## Before finishing
Run `npm run build`, `npm run lint` and `npm run typecheck` and report deltas.
`lint` is at zero errors — keep it there. `typecheck` has a known backlog of ~150
JS-inference errors (see AGENTS.md); do not paper over it by turning off `checkJs`,
and do not let the count grow.

## Authorization reality
RLS is the only auth boundary for CRM data (browser-direct PostgREST + anon key).
Treat role/subscription/MFA checks in React as UX only, not security.
